 See the [API reference documentation](https://docs.page/invertase/denque/api) for more examples.
 
+## API
+
+### `rotate(steps = 1): this`
+
+Rotates the queue in place and returns the queue. Positive `steps` move values
+from the back to the front; negative `steps` move values from the front to the
+back. Steps must be finite integers and are normalized by the current queue
+length.
+
+```js
+const denque = new Denque([1, 2, 3, 4]);
+denque.rotate(); // [4, 1, 2, 3]
+denque.rotate(-1); // [1, 2, 3, 4]
+```
+
