+### `rotate(steps = 1)` -> `Denque`
+
+Rotates this queue in place and returns it. Positive `steps` move values from
+the back to the front; negative `steps` move values from the front to the back.
+Steps must be finite integers and are normalized by the current queue length.
+
+```js
+var denque = new Denque([1,2,3,4]);
+denque.rotate(); // [4,1,2,3]
+denque.rotate(-1); // [1,2,3,4]
+```
+
+
+
 ### `toArray()` -> `Array`
 
 Returns the items in the queue as an array. Starting from the item in the front of the queue and ending to the item at the back of the queue.
